															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/timetravelinc" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2269412); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2269412&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609818764" alt="TimeTravelinc" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2269412)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/timetravelinc" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2269412); return false;" >TimeTravelinc</a></span> <span class="odate time_1496849251 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">07 Jun 2017 15:27</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2845377">
									

<p>So, is this somewhat connected to an idea? Because what you're describing to me is items that somehow was or were existing, which then suddenly became non-existent If that's so, is it like &quot;House of Leaves&quot;?</p>
<p>Because in the book, Zampano<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-15672-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-15672-1')">1</a></sup>, (who originally wrote part of the book) mentions a movie that doesn't exist called <em>The Navidson Record</em><sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-15672-2" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-15672-2')">2</a></sup>. As it happens, Zampano references books and articles that also don't exist and the one who found the manuscript <tt>Johnny Truant</tt>, mentions this, as well as write too much in the footnotes<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-15672-3" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-15672-3')">3</a></sup>.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-15672-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-15672-1')">1</a>. <em>possibly italian or spanish</em></div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-15672-2"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-15672-2')">2</a>. The movie in question describes a connection involving a house, expanding it's interiors but not the exteriors (adding doors, expanding the interior by 1/4&quot;, then by 5/16&quot;, etc. etc.), and the strange events following</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-15672-3"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-15672-3')">3</a>. I mean seriously, he writes a lot, involving his own personal story, and how it interweaves with a manuscript, and a non-existent film about a house expanding into a maze.</div>
</div>

							</div>

								
					
