					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wrongjohnsilver" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2000367); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2000367&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609818764" alt="WrongJohnSilver" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2000367)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/wrongjohnsilver" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(2000367); return false;" >WrongJohnSilver</a></span> <span class="odate time_1472570251 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">30 Aug 2016 15:17</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2580855">
									

<p>Let me preface this by pointing out that I was asked and wanted to critique this in its earlier stages, but did and could not.</p>
<p>There are more narratives that can be constructed from this one, thanks to the rampant numerology. It's a metanarrative to a concept that reaches through the first six to find the seventh tantalizingly out of reach&#8230; just yet.</p>
<p>Furthermore, the constant theme of effort resulting in never reaching the goal, an outpouring of toil leading to no actual progress&#8230; Let's just say that it's been a recurring theme in some of my works.</p>
<p>The infinite asypmtotic approach to finality, the singularity that you can get ever closer to, yet never precisely reach. The fractal spiral.</p>
<p>Where have we seen these before? In many places, throughout the wiki.</p>
<p><em>That</em> is the (trembling) core of the awakening.</p>
<p><span style="color: #fcfcfc">Would you like the on-mount-golgotha tag?</span></p>

